# Web frontend

- `src/core/` is pure TypeScript. It must not import React, Konva, or three.js.
- Konva draws. Hit targets and tools call core operations. Tools are state machines, not boolean piles on the stage.
- Plan Y is up. Convert to screen Y in one view module.
- Picking uses `rbush`. Undo uses `immer` patches. Wall polygons use `polygon-clipping`.
- Autosave on pointer-up or a short debounce, never on every pointer-move. Send the revision. A 409 reloads the plan and shows an error.
- PDF and SVG come from `src/drawing/` draw commands, not from a screenshot of the canvas.

```typescript
// Bad: core importing the canvas
import { Line } from "react-konva";

// Good: core returns points, the canvas maps them
const poly = wallPolygon(wall, joins);
```
